# g(a, y) = (x*4 + y mod 4) div 4, with x = a mod 100.
# Bounds: x is in [0, 99], so x*4 is in [0, 396] and cannot wrap; y mod 4 is in [0, 3].
# So the remainder never carries into the quotient, and g simplifies to x.
# Check with a = -3, y = 7: x = -3 mod 100 = 97 (floor), 97*4 + 7 mod 4 = 388 + 3 = 391, 391 div 4 = 97.
%a    = param [] slot=0 dtype=i32
%y    = param [] slot=1 dtype=i32
%x    = mod %a 100
%g    = div (add (mul %x 4) (mod %y 4)) 4
%r    = call %g -3 7
%test = assert %r 97
